postgres-db                | 	NoSQL
postgres-db                | 	Azure Cosmos DB is a NoSQL (Not only SQL) database, which means it can handle unstructured, semi-structured, structured, and vector data types. 
postgres-db                | 	Vector database
postgres-db                | 	Azure Cosmos DB is a vector database that can handle large-scale vector data. 
postgres-db                | 	Multiple APIs
postgres-db                | 	Azure Cosmos DB offers multiple database APIs, including NoSQL, MongoDB, PostgreSQL, Cassandra, Gremlin, and Table. 
postgres-db                | 	Physical partitions
postgres-db                | 	The underlying storage mechanism for data in Azure Cosmos DB is called a physical partition. 
postgres-db                | 	Logical partitions
postgres-db                | 	Azure Cosmos DB abstracts the partitioning concept with a logical partition. 
postgres-db                | 	Built-in vector search
postgres-db                | 	Azure Cosmos DB offers built-in vector search to query vectors and relevant data efficiently. 
postgres-db                | 	SLA-backed availability
postgres-db                | 	Azure Cosmos DB offers SLA-backed 99.999 percent availability for NoSQL data. 
postgres-db                | 	Serverless or autoscale options
postgres-db                | 	Azure Cosmos DB offers serverless or autoscale options to pay for only what you use. 
postgres-db                | 	Azure Cosmos DB is designed to provide:
postgres-db                | 	High availability
postgres-db                | 	Scalability
postgres-db                | 	Low-latency access to data
postgres-db                | 	Single-digit millisecond response times
postgres-db                | 	Automatic and instant scalability
